WEBVTT

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.940
I have seen ABC today for her pre-operator visit for weight management.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:10.180
I have explained to her the need for Optifast for weight loss prior to these procedures

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:13.400
to make it safer because of the large size of her liver.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:14.820
She understands this.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:27.260
Impression plan. We are going to put her on two weeks of Optifast at around 900 calories. I have also explained the risks and potential complications of laparoscopic colosyctomy to

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:32.520
her in detail including bleeding, infection, deep venous, thrombosis, pulmonary embolism,

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.480
injury to the small intestine, stomach, liver, leak from the cystic duct, common bile duct

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:44.300
and possible need for ERCPA and further surgery. This surgery is going to be planned for October 6.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.180
This is for Kolelothiasis prior to her lab banning procedure.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:58.980
I have also reviewed with her the risks and potential complications of laparoscopic gastric banning including bleeding, infection, deep venous, thrombosis, pulmonary embolism,

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:04.720
leakage of the band, erosion of the band, injury to the esophagus, stomach and small

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.540
intestine, large intestine, spleen, liver, injury to the band, port or tubing, necessitating

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.040
replacement of the band or porting a tubing among other potential complications and

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:15.680
she understands.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.460
We are going to proceed for laparoscopic gastric banning.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.980
I have reviewed her entire chart in detail.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:27.740
I have also gone over with her the Fairfield Country Bariatric Concern Form for

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.320
banding and all the risks.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:35.660
She has also signed the St. Vincent Hospital Concern Form for lap banding.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:43.900
She has taken the pre-operative quiz for banding. She has assigned the pre-op and post-op instructions and understands them and we reviewed them.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.380
She has taken the quiz and done fairly well.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:51.280
We have reviewed with her any potential other issues and I have answered her questions.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.020
She has also planned for surgical intervention.
